WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:02.130
New Zealand calls state of emergency over
torrential flooding | DW News

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:05.170
New Zealand's military has been called in
to help evacuate hundreds of people caught

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:07.240
in flooding in the country's South Island.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:11.220
A state of emergency has been declared in
the Canterbury region that surrounds the city

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:13.480
of Christchurch.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:18.430
As much as 40 centimeters of rain has fallen
in the area over the last two days.

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:24.039
Meteorologists say that in some areas, that's
more than the entire rainfall so far this

00:00:24.039 --> 00:00:26.710
year.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:30.579
The extent of the flooding.

00:00:30.579 --> 00:00:34.490
Houses marooned by water.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:44.460
Roads impassable -
This one left with a gaping hole.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:48.450
And rivers have turned into lakes.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:54.990
"Well, I went to bed about 10 o'clock last
night and there was not a sign of the river.

00:00:54.990 --> 00:01:01.900
Get up at 6 o'clock this morning and it's
gone, half of the farm is underwater."

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:06.900
The Canterbury region on New Zealand's South
Island is a farming hub.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:13.939
But the deluge of rain is making work hard
- even if some are putting on a brave face.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:16.729
"Just carried on, just carried on.

00:01:16.729 --> 00:01:18.579
Can't worry about it.

00:01:18.579 --> 00:01:25.970
You know you just got to pour water on or
just farm to the conditions."

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:31.490
But conditions have left some in extreme danger.

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:38.540
On Sunday, this man was airlifted to safety
after becoming trapped in flood water.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:42.380
"It has been a really delicate rescue, very
lucky.

00:01:42.380 --> 00:01:46.600
We tried a rescue helicopter earlier, but
they couldn't get through because of the weather,

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:52.090
so it's just been a really good outcome for
everybody and well done to the chopper crew."

00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:59.240
Here, rescue workers are trying to reach a
car that's fallen down the cliff just above

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:03.030
the raging river.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:07.009
Hundreds of people have been evacuated from
their homes.

00:02:07.009 --> 00:02:12.970
Authorities have now declared a state of emergency
with more rain expected.

